# Backend API Guidelines

## Server Structure
- Main server: [server/server.js](mdc:server/server.js)
- Routes: [server/routes/optimizedRoutes.js](mdc:server/routes/optimizedRoutes.js)
- Middleware: [server/middleware/](mdc:server/middleware/)
- Services: [server/services/](mdc:server/services/)

## Key Features
- Cookie-based authentication
- WebSocket real-time updates
- Rate limiting and security
- Performance monitoring
- GDPR compliance

## API Endpoints
- `/api/timetable` - Timetable CRUD operations
- `/api/news` - News management
- `/api/city-tips` - City recommendations
- `/api/participants` - Participant management
- `/api/links` - Important links

## Validation
- Use [server/middleware/validation.js](mdc:server/middleware/validation.js)
- Timetable types: `team-round`, `individual-round`, `workshop`, `fun`, `aftershow`
- Implement proper error handling
- Use structured logging

## Database Integration
- Use hybrid data service for API calls
- Implement WebSocket subscriptions
- Handle real-time updates
- Maintain data consistency
